  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prevention of Human Trafficking &amp; Modern Day Slavery in Nepal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recently launched Australia&#x2019;s international engagement strategy on human trafficking and modern slavery: Delivering in partnership has a vision of a future where no one is subjected to human trafficking and other forms of modern slavery and the human rights of all are valued equally. 
The strategy has committed that Australia will continue to work with foreign counterparts, businesses, and civil society to increase awareness of, and help end, the human rights abuses of human trafficking, forced labour and forced marriage.
The document has identified, among others, weak rule of law as drivers of human trafficking and modern slavery.
In this backdrop, Post received an Overseas Development Aid (ODA) allocation of $547,336 for delivering high quality projects on anti-human trafficking and modern-day slavery activities.</narrative>
  </description>
